{"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"FloatingPointFormatStyle","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FloatingPointFormatStyle"}],"symbolKind":"struct","platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"12.0","beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false}],"modules":[{"name":"FoundationInternationalization"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FloatingPointFormatStyle"}],"externalID":"s:30FoundationInternationalization24FloatingPointFormatStyleV","role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FloatingPointFormatStyle"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SB","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Instances of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" create localized, human-readable text from ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint","type":"text"},{"text":" numbers and parse string representations of numbers into instances of ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint","type":"text"},{"text":" types. All of the Swift standard library’s floating-point types, such as ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/double","type":"text"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/float","type":"text"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/float80","type":"text"},{"text":", conform to ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint","type":"text"},{"text":", and therefore work with this format style.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" includes two nested types, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Percent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Currency","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", for working with percentages and currencies, respectively. Each format style includes a configuration that determines how it represents numeric values, for things like grouping, displaying signs, and variant presentations like scientific notation. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Percent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" include a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/NumberFormatStyleConfiguration","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/Currency","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" includes a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/CurrencyFormatStyleConfiguration","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". You can customize numeric formatting for a style by adjusting its backing configuration. The system automatically caches unique configurations of a format style to enhance performance.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Foundation provides another format style type, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/IntegerFormatStyle","type":"reference"},{"text":", for working with numbers that conform to ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryinteger","type":"text"},{"text":". For Foundation’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Decimal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"Decimal\/FormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Formatting floating-point values","anchor":"Formatting-floating-point-values","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint\/formatted()","type":"text"},{"text":" method to create a string representation of a floating-point value using the default ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" configuration.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let formattedDefault = 12345.67.formatted()","\/\/ formattedDefault is \"12,345.67\" in the en_US locale.","\/\/ Other locales may use different separator and grouping behavior."],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can specify a format style by providing an argument to the ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint\/formatted(_:)-4ksqj","type":"text"},{"text":" method. The following example shows the number ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represented in each of the available styles, in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"en_US","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" locale:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let number = 0.1","","let formattedNumber = number.formatted(.number)","\/\/ formattedNumber is \"0.1\".","","let formattedPercent = number.formatted(.percent)","\/\/ formattedPercent is \"10%\".","","let formattedCurrency = number.formatted(.currency(code: \"USD\"))","\/\/ formattedCurrency is \"$0.10\"."],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each style provides methods for updating its numeric configuration, including the number of significant digits, grouping length, and more. You can specify a numeric configuration by calling as many of these methods as you need in any order you choose. The following example shows the same number with default and custom configurations:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let exampleNumber = 123456.78","","let defaultFormatting = exampleNumber.formatted(.number)","\/\/ defaultFormatting is \"123 456,78\" for the \"fr_FR\" locale.","\/\/ defaultFormatting is \"123,456.78\" for the \"en_US\" locale.","","let customFormatting = exampleNumber.formatted(",".number",".grouping(.never)",".sign(strategy: .always()))","\/\/ customFormatting is \"+123456.78\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Creating a floating-point format style instance","anchor":"Creating-a-floating-point-format-style-instance","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The previous examples use static factory methods like ","type":"text"},{"code":"FormatStyle\/number-8c8rj","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to create format styles within the call to the ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/swift\/binaryfloatingpoint\/formatted(_:)-4ksqj","type":"text"},{"text":" method. You can also create a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" instance and use it to repeatedly format different values, with the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle\/format(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let percentFormatStyle = FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>.Percent()","","percentFormatStyle.format(0.5) \/\/ \"50%\"","percentFormatStyle.format(0.855) \/\/ \"85.5%\"","percentFormatStyle.format(1.0) \/\/ \"100%\"",""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Parsing floating-point values","anchor":"Parsing-floating-point-values","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/documentation\/FoundationInternationalization\/FloatingPointFormatStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to parse strings into floating-point values. You can define the format style within the type’s initializer or pass in a format style created outside the function, as shown here:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let price = try? Double(\"$3,500.63\",","format: .currency(code: \"USD\")) \/\/ 3500.63","","let priceFormatStyle = FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>.Currency(code: \"USD\")","let salePrice = try? Double(\"$731.67\",","format: priceFormatStyle) \/\/ 731.67"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Matching regular expressions","anchor":"Matching-regular-expressions","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Along with parsing numeric values in strings, you can use theSwift regular expression domain-specific language to match and capture numeric substrings. The following example defines a percentage format style to match a percentage value using ","type":"text"},{"code":"en_US","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" numeric conventions. The rest of the regular expression ignores any characters prior to a ","type":"text"},{"code":"\": \"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sequence that precedes the percentage substring.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import RegexBuilder","let source = \"Percentage complete: 55.1%\"","let matcher = Regex {","OneOrMore(.any)","\": \"","Capture {","One(.localizedDoublePercentage(locale: Locale(identifier: \"en_US\")))","}","}","let match = source.firstMatch(of: matcher)","let localizedPercentage = match?.1","print(\"\\(localizedPercentage!)\") \/\/ 0.551"],"syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/20FoundationEssentials11FormatStyleP","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/20FoundationEssentials20ParseableFormatStyleP","doc:\/\/FoundationInternationalization\/s8Copy